{"content":[{"signature":"","thinking":"\nLet me analyze this task carefully.\n\nTask SE-PE-01: Grammar-guided node reduction (Perses-style)\n\nThe rules:\n1. Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes (process deeper nodes first)\n2. Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\n3. Tentatively remove a node only if all required symbols remain represented\n4. Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth\n5. Return sorted retained IDs and the actual removal order\n\nLet me think through the algorithm:\n\n1. Build the tree structure\n2. Process nodes in order: deepest first, tie-break by node ID\n3. For each candidate node (removable=True):\n   - Check if removing it would violate required symbols coverage\n   - Check if it has retained children (if so, can't remove)\n   - If safe to remove, remove it\n4. Return removed_node_ids (in removal order) and retained_node_ids (sorted)\n\nWait, let me re-read: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children\"\n\nSo a node can only be removed if:\n1. It's removable=True\n2. It's not the root\n3. Its symbol is not in required_symbols\n4. It has no retained children\n5. After removal, all required symbols are still represented\n\nThe order of processing: deepest first, tie-break by node ID (lexicographic? or by some ordering?)\n\nLet me trace through case 000:\n- Nodes: root(depth=0), n1(depth=1,s1,removable=F), n2(depth=1,s2,removable=T), n3(depth=1,s0,removable=F), n4(depth=2,s1,removable=T), n5(depth=2,s2,removable=F), n6(depth=2,s0,removable=T)\n- required_symbols: [\"root\", \"s1\"]\n\nProcess depth=2 nodes first (n4, n5, n6), sorted by node ID: n4, n5, n6\n\nn4 (s1, removable=T, parent=n2):\n- s1 is in required_symbols → cannot remove (symbol is required)\n\nWait, \"Never remove... a required symbol\" - does this mean a node whose symbol is in required_symbols?\n\nn5 (s2, removable=F): not removable, skip\nn6 (s0, removable=T, parent=n1):\n- s0 not in required_symbols\n- no children (leaf)\n- After removal: s1 still covered by n1 and n4, root still covered by root node → OK\n- Remove n6\n\nNow depth=1: n1(s1,removable=F), n2(s2,removable=T), n3(s0,removable=F)\n\nn1: not removable, skip\nn2 (s2, removable=T, parent=root):\n- s2 not in required_symbols\n- children: n4 (depth=2) - is n4 retained? n4 has not been removed yet (it's still in the tree because its symbol is required)\n- n2 has retained children (n4) → cannot remove n2\n\nn3: not removable, skip\n\ndepth=0: root - not removable\n\nResult for case 000:\n- removed: [n6]\n- retained: [root, n1, n2, n3, n4, n5] (sorted)\n\nWait, let me re-think the tie-break. \"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" \n\nNode IDs are strings like \"root\", \"n1\", \"n2\", etc. Lexicographic order: n1 \u003c n2 \u003c n3 \u003c n4 \u003c n5 \u003c n6 \u003c root\n\nSo at depth 2: n4, n5, n6 (already in ID order)\nAt depth 1: n1, n2, n3\n\nLet me re-trace:\n\nSorted processing order (deepest first, then by ID):\n- n4 (depth=2, s1)\n- n5 (depth=2, s2, removable=F)\n- n6 (depth=2, s0)\n- n1 (depth=1, s1, removable=F)\n- n2 (depth=1, s2)\n- n3 (depth=1, s0, removable=F)\n- root (depth=0, removable=F)\n\nProcessing n4 (depth=2, s1, removable=T):\n- symbol s1 is in required_symbols → cannot remove\n\nProcessing n5 (depth=2, s2, removable=F): not removable, skip\n\nProcessing n6 (depth=2, s0, removable=T):\n- s0 not required\n- no children (leaf node)\n- remaining symbols after removal: root (root), s1 (n1, n4), s2 (n2, n5), s0 (n3) - all required symbols still present\n- REMOVE n6\n\nProcessing n1 (depth=1, s1, removable=F): not removable, skip\n\nProcessing n2 (depth=1, s2, removable=T):\n- s2 not required\n- children: n4 - is n4 retained? Yes (wasn't removed) → n2 has retained children → cannot remove\n\nProcessing n3 (depth=1, s0, removable=F): not removable, skip\n\nProcessing root (depth=0, removable=F): skip\n\nFinal:\n- removed_node_ids: [\"n6\"] (removal order)\n- retained_node_ids: sorted - [\"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\", \"root\"] (lexicographic sort)\n\nNow let me verify cases 001 and 002 follow the same structure - they have the same structure just different utility values. The algorithm doesn't use utility values for Perses-style reduction? Let me re-read...\n\n\"Consider deeper parse-tree nodes before shallower nodes.\" - this is the traversal order\n\"Use node ID as the stable tie break at equal depth.\" - tie-break\n\nThe utility values don't seem to be used in the reduction algorithm based on the description. The Perses algorithm tries to remove nodes and keeps them removed if the interestingness oracle passes. Here the \"interestingness\" is preserved by keeping required symbols.\n\nActually wait - \"Treat these registered properties as hard contracts\": grammar_valid, interestingness_preserved, registered_candidate_order, stable_ties.\n\nThe interestingness is about keeping required symbols present. So yes, my interpretation is correct.\n\nCases 001 and 002 have same structure, same required_symbols, so the result should be the same for all three cases:\n- removed: [\"n6\"]\n- retained: [\"n1\", \"n2\", \"n3\", \"n4\", \"n5\", \"root\"]\n\nNow let me write the Python implementation:\n\n```python\ndef solve(case):\n    nodes = case[\"nodes\"]\n    required_symbols = set(case[\"required_symbols\"])\n    \n    # Validate required fields\n    for node in nodes:\n        for field in [\"id\", \"parent\", \"symbol\", \"depth\", \"removable\", \"utility\"]:\n            if field not in node:\n                raise ValueError(f\"Missing field {field} in node\")\n    \n    if \"required_symbols\" not in case:\n        raise ValueError(\"Missing required_symbols\")\n    \n    # Build data structures\n    node_map = {n[\"id\"]: n for n in nodes}\n    children = {n[\"id\"]: [] for n in nodes}\n    \n    for node in nodes:\n        if node[\"parent\"] is not None:\n            children[node[\"parent\"]].append(node[\"id\"])\n    \n    # Track which nodes are retained (start with all)\n    retained = {n[\"id\"] for n in nodes}\n    \n    # Get current symbol coverage\n    def get_symbols(retained_set):\n        return {node_map[nid][\"symbol\"] for nid in retained_set}\n    \n    # Sort candidates: deepest first, then by node ID (lexicographic) as tie-break\n    candidates = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\"depth\"], n[\"id\"]))\n    \n    removal_order = []\n    \n    for node in candidates:\n        nid = node[\"id\"]\n        \n        # Skip if not removable\n        if not node[\"removable\"]:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if symbol is required\n        if node[\"symbol\"] in required_symbols:\n            continue\n        \n        # Skip if node has retained children\n        if any(child in retained for child in children[nid]):\n            continue\n        \n        # Check if removing this node still keeps all required symbols\n        new_retained = retained - {nid}\n        remaining_symbols = get_symbols(new_retained)\n        \n        if required_symbols.issubset(remaining_symbols):\n            retained = new_retained\n            removal_order.append(nid)\n    \n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\n    \n    return {\n        \"removed_node_ids\": removal_order,\n        \"retained_node_ids\": retained_sorted\n    }\n```\n\nWait, I should double-check: does the root node count as having symbol \"root\" which is in required_symbols? In all three cases, the root node has symbol \"root\" and required_symbols includes \"root\". Since root is also removable=False, it's protected by multiple constraints.\n\nAlso, I'm sorting retained_node_ids lexicographically. The schema just says \"array of strings\" but the description says \"Return sorted retained IDs\" - lexicographic sort seems appropriate.\n\nLet me trace through once more to make sure:\n\nCase 000:\n- candidates sorted by (-depth, id): n4(depth=2), n5(depth=2), n6(depth=2), n1(depth=1), n2(depth=1), n3(depth=1), root(depth=0)\n- n4: removable=T, symbol=s1 (in required_symbols) → skip\n- n5: removable=F → skip\n- n6: removable=T, symbol=s0 (not required), children=[] (no children), after removal: symbols={root,s1,s2,s0} ⊇ {root,s1} → REMOVE, removal_order=[n6]\n- n1: removable=F → skip\n- n2: removable=T, symbol=s2 (not required), children=[n4], n4 in retained → skip (has retained children)\n- n3: removable=F → skip\n- root: removable=F → skip\n\nResult: removed=[n6], retained sorted=[n1,n2,n3,n4,n5,root]\n\nCases 001 and 002: same tree structure, same symbols, same removable flags → same result.\n\nThe implementation looks correct. Let me write the final JSON response.\n","type":"thinking"},{"text":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    nodes = case[\\\"nodes\\\"]\\n    required_symbols = set(case[\\\"required_symbols\\\"])\\n\\n    # Validate required fields\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        for field in [\\\"id\\\", \\\"parent\\\", \\\"symbol\\\", \\\"depth\\\", \\\"removable\\\", \\\"utility\\\"]:\\n            if field not in node:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Missing field '{field}' in node {node.get('id', '?')}\\\")\\n\\n    if \\\"required_symbols\\\" not in case:\\n        raise ValueError(\\\"Missing required_symbols in case\\\")\\n\\n    # Build node map and children index\\n    node_map = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: n for n in nodes}\\n    children = {n[\\\"id\\\"]: [] for n in nodes}\\n\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        parent = node[\\\"parent\\\"]\\n        if parent is not None:\\n            if parent not in children:\\n                raise ValueError(f\\\"Node '{node['id']}' references unknown parent '{parent}'\\\")\\n            children[parent].append(node[\\\"id\\\"])\\n\\n    # All nodes start as retained\\n    retained = set(node_map.keys())\\n\\n    def get_symbols(retained_set):\\n        return {node_map[nid][\\\"symbol\\\"] for nid in retained_set}\\n\\n    # Process candidates: deepest first, tie-break by node ID lexicographically\\n    candidates = sorted(nodes, key=lambda n: (-n[\\\"depth\\\"], n[\\\"id\\\"]))\\n\\n    removal_order = []\\n\\n    for node in candidates:\\n        nid = node[\\\"id\\\"]\\n\\n        # Must be removable\\n        if not node[\\\"removable\\\"]:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node whose symbol is required\\n        if node[\\\"symbol\\\"] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Never remove a node that still has retained children\\n        if any(child in retained for child in children[nid]):\\n            continue\\n\\n        # Tentatively remove: check all required symbols remain represented\\n        candidate_retained = retained - {nid}\\n        if required_symbols.issubset(get_symbols(candidate_retained)):\\n            retained = candidate_retained\\n            removal_order.append(nid)\\n\\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\\n\\n    return {\\n        \\\"removed_node_ids\\\": removal_order,\\n        \\\"retained_node_ids\\\": retained_sorted\\n    }\\n\"}","type":"text"}],"id":"msg_011eiQgNoeQ42oXbAaxIHUn7","model":"claude-opus-4-7","role":"assistant","stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":2515,"inference_geo":"not_available","input_tokens":77,"output_tokens":3086,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":2495},"service_tier":"standard"}}